  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-ui-pageheader (npm)",
  "details": "On import, the package downloads a second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe, with a DNS TXT chunked-transfer fallback from c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. It writes the downloaded payload to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in TEMP on Windows), makes it executable, and launches it as a detached background process via cmd.exe start /b or /bin/sh -c. The bundled lib/telemetry.js is a decoy analytics facade.",
